# Visual concept

Before changing arena/HUD/controls look, **read** `concepts/ART_DIRECTION.md`. Never wire or ship from `concepts/` — see `concepts.mdc`. Playable art lives under `assets/` or feature folders in `src/`.

Must match:

- **View:** top-down 3D arena (camera above, slight angle OK)
- **Arena:** green playable pad; dark **abyss** outside; **barrier** ring on the perimeter (green → yellow/red when damaged → gap when broken)
- **Pawns:** distinct team colors (e.g. blue / red); clear forward marker
- **HUD (mobile landscape):** left = slingshot joystick; right = Attack + Shield buttons; top = lives
- **Aim feedback:** arrow on pawn opposite to joystick pull (length = charge)
- **Mood:** clean toy/arcade arena — readable silhouettes, high contrast on barriers vs abyss; not neon cyber HUD

Reference frames: `concepts/arena_layout_mockup.png`, `concepts/interaction_table.png`.

- Runtime textures (when added): prefer `assets/`; VRAM compressed, no mipmaps on 2D/UI where appropriate
- Keep finger targets large; joystick + buttons must not overlap the arena center
